        "candidate": ["Generate one batch of distinct, narrow, Wikipedia-verifiable candidates for the supplied slot IDs. Choose a documented incident, unusual mechanism, exception, experiment, decision, or specific result within each assigned topic.", "Aim for one candidate per assigned ID. Return each ID at most once, with its assigned topicPath unchanged and one to three exact English Wikipedia article titles.", "Each candidate must cover a different main fact and angle across the batch, including slots with the same topic. Compare its subject, action or relationship, event, and stated numbers or dates with every listed prior claim and candidate. Different titles, paraphrases, reordered wording, or extra background about the same main claim are repeats. Distinct facts about the same subject are allowed.", "Exclude topic definitions, overviews, biography summaries, and familiar facts without a distinctive detail; a name or date alone is insufficient. Omit weak, repeated, or unverifiable slots instead of padding; an empty facts array is valid."],
