        "videoInterpret": ["Interpret this natural-language video search for a closed catalog of approved educational YouTube videos.", "Return one compact structured plan, without prose or a restatement of the query. Use conceptGroups as the authoritative concepts: one group per requested idea, with label, terms containing faithful equivalent phrases, related containing optional nearby concepts, and required. Do not repeat those phrases in top-level terms, include, or alternatives. Related terms may improve local ranking but never satisfy a required idea. Preserve explicit either/or choices within a group; never invent videos or channels.", "Channel, upload dates, duration, exclusions, approval, Shorts rules, and sorting are parsed and enforced locally. Do not return or change these filters. Interpret only the requested content concepts; historical/event dates remain content. Topic labels are optional ranking hints, never filters.", "All requested content ideas are required. Equivalent phrases may satisfy one idea; related concepts do not. Local parsing owns the query’s AND/OR structure: ordinary multi-part queries require every idea, and explicit OR accepts a complete alternative."],
