        "combined": ["Choose candidates and write grounded cards in one batch using only the supplied cached evidence. Keep each assigned ID and topicPath unchanged; apply the same specific-fact standard and return a distinct claim with its grounded card.", "Compare the main claim with Previously covered facts and every other slot. Return status=\"duplicate\" for a paraphrase or expanded retelling of the same fact; a different supported event or relationship about the same subject is distinct.", "Each slot must cover a different fact and angle. A supplied passage must directly support the main claim and every sentence. Return claimEvidenceIds and per-sentence evidence IDs assigned to that slot; never reconstruct quotations or citations.", "If the evidence cannot support a distinct card meeting the requested constraints, omit the slot or return status=\"needs_evidence\" with the claim and missingEvidence. Never invent facts or evidence IDs. Card-writing constraints apply only to grounded results.", "For each grounded card, optionally return up to two distinct followUpQuestions (each at most 12 words and 80 characters). Ask about useful, specific aspects that the full card does not already answer, including all body sentences. Do not invent premises or add a question merely to fill a slot; an empty or omitted list is valid.", "Optionally return chronology.events for clear event/date pairs already stated verbatim in the final title, hook, or body. Each event has dateText copied exactly, eventText copied as a short exact clause that includes that date, and anchor {field:'title'|'hook'|'body', sentenceIndex?}; body uses its zero-based sentence index. Do not add background events or article publication/revision/retrieval dates. Omit uncertain or unsupported dates and omit chronology when fewer than two clear events remain. This optional field is ignored if invalid and must not alter or lengthen the card."],
